---
import FaqBlock from '../components/FaqBlock.astro';
import GuideCard from '../components/GuideCard.astro';
import SourcePanel from '../components/SourcePanel.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../data/assets';
import { CORE_SOURCES } from '../data/sources';
import { OFFICIAL_FACTS, REQUIRED_GUIDES, SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Grave Seasons Guide - Romance, Walkthrough & Characters';
const description =
  'Official-source Grave Seasons guide for romance, walkthrough, characters, quests, and tips. Built from Steam and Blumhouse data, with launch-day updates clearly separated.';
const homeFaqs = [
  {
    question: 'When does Grave Seasons release?',
    answer:
      'Fall 2026, with no exact day locked. Perfect Garbage originally announced August 14, 2026, then posted on 5 June 2026 that they were moving the release date of the full game to Fall of this year, across all announced platforms. Blumhouse Games lists the same Fall 2026 window while the Steam store field still shows only 2026. This site uses Fall 2026 as the official launch window and avoids inventing a specific day until Steam, Blumhouse, PlayStation, or Microsoft publishes one. That source discipline matters because release-date pages can age quickly; every date update should keep the store text, publisher text, and verification date visible for readers. If the studio later posts a trailer, press release, or storefront update with a more exact date, that item should be linked from the sources panel before the homepage headline changes.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Grave Seasons on Game Pass?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Perfect Garbage stated in their official Steam announcement that Grave Seasons will also be released on Day 1 for Xbox Game Pass players, alongside the four-platform launch list. The 5 June 2026 delay post kept all announced platforms, so the Day 1 Game Pass commitment still stands for the Fall 2026 window. What has not been specified is which Game Pass tiers are included, whether cloud or PC Game Pass is covered separately, or how long the title stays in the catalogue. The platforms page tracks the exact wording and its date, and will separate launch access from any later preorder, pricing, or edition details rather than blending them into one claim.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many romance options are in Grave Seasons?',
    answer:
      'Steam states that Grave Seasons includes 12 potential romanceable people. The same official description also says a few romanceable folks may have the potential to be the killer, which makes the romance system part of the murder mystery rather than a separate side activity. The full route names, gift preferences, heart events, marriage rules, and dialogue choices have not been officially published yet, so the romance guide keeps a verified framework now and will separate launch-day findings from pre-launch facts. After release, each romance route should list version notes and spoiler labels because killer selection can change story context.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Grave Seasons multiplayer?',
    answer:
      'The official pages checked for this site do not confirm multiplayer, co-op, or online shared-farm features. Steam, Blumhouse, PlayStation, and Microsoft listings are useful for platform and release-window verification, but this guide does not convert missing feature text into a promise either way. Until an official page lists multiplayer support or the released game exposes it directly, the safe SEO answer is that multiplayer status is unconfirmed and the current guide focuses on the confirmed farming, relationship, and murder mystery structure. If feature tags change, this answer should quote the updated platform source rather than paraphrase rumors.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What platforms is Grave Seasons on?',
    answer:
      'Four, named directly in Perfect Garbage\'s official announcement: PC, Xbox Series X|S, PlayStation 5, and Nintendo Switch. Live store listings currently exist for Steam, the PlayStation Store, and the Microsoft Store, and Xbox Game Pass access is confirmed for day one. A Nintendo eShop listing is not tracked yet even though the platform itself is confirmed, and no Xbox One or Switch 2 version has been mentioned. The platforms page keeps those official links together and leaves room for store-specific updates when the publisher or platform holders publish more complete launch information. It still declines to guess at release parity, performance modes, or edition details, because none of those has been stated. That keeps platform SEO useful for searchers without turning the site into a rumor mirror.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="home" fullWidth image={ASSETS.hero.src}>
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden border-b border-white/10">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <img
        src={ASSETS.hero.src}
        alt={ASSETS.hero.alt}
        width={ASSETS.hero.width}
        height={ASSETS.hero.height}
        class="h-full w-full object-cover object-center"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="sync"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-ink/65"></div>
      <div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-56 bg-gradient-to-t from-ink to-transparent"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container relative flex min-h-[78vh] flex-col justify-center py-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="section-kicker">Official-source fan guide</p>
        <img
          src={ASSETS.title.src}
          alt={ASSETS.title.alt}
          width={ASSETS.title.width}
          height={ASSETS.title.height}
          class="mt-5 max-h-48 w-auto"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="sync"
        />
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-bone md:text-6xl">
          Grave Seasons Guide
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-bone">
          Romance tracking, walkthrough framework, resident notes, quest planning, and spoiler-aware launch updates for Ashenridge.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/romance-guide/" class="btn-primary">Romance guide</a>
          <a href="/walkthrough/" class="btn-secondary">Walkthrough hub</a>
          <a href={SITE.steamUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" class="btn-secondary">Steam page</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-kicker">Current verified state</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">No route claims until the game data exists</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-fog">
        Grave Seasons is not released yet. This site uses Steam, Blumhouse, PlayStation, and Microsoft store information for pre-launch pages, then separates launch-day walkthrough updates from confirmed official facts.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="surface p-5">
          <dt class="text-xs font-black uppercase text-wheat">Release window</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-bone">{SITE.releaseWindow}</dd>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-fog">Steam currently lists {SITE.steamReleaseText}.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="surface p-5">
          <dt class="text-xs font-black uppercase text-wheat">Developer</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-bone">{SITE.developer}</dd>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-fog">Publisher: {SITE.publisher}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="surface p-5">
          <dt class="text-xs font-black uppercase text-wheat">Romance scope</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-bone">12 options</dd>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-fog">Steam says a few may be the killer.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="surface p-5">
          <dt class="text-xs font-black uppercase text-wheat">Town scope</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-xl font-black text-bone">30+ residents</dd>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-fog">Steam lists 70+ interior locations.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">SEO guide map</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Start with the core pages</h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/characters/" class="text-sm font-bold text-wheat hover:text-bone">Open character tracker</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {REQUIRED_GUIDES.map((guide) => (
          <GuideCard href={guide.href} title={guide.title} description={guide.description} label={guide.priority} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="container grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Ashenridge facts</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">What official pages already confirm</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
          {OFFICIAL_FACTS.map((fact) => (
            <div class="border-l-2 border-wheat/45 pl-4">
              <h3 class="font-black text-bone">{fact.label}</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">{fact.value}</p>
              <a href={fact.source.url} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" class="mt-1 inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase text-wheat">
                Source: {fact.source.label}
              </a>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <img
          src={ASSETS.farmHarvest.src}
          alt={ASSETS.farmHarvest.alt}
          width={ASSETS.farmHarvest.width}
          height={ASSETS.farmHarvest.height}
          class="rounded-md border border-white/10"
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.farmHarvest.credit}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <figure>
          <img src={ASSETS.townNight.src} alt={ASSETS.townNight.alt} width={ASSETS.townNight.width} height={ASSETS.townNight.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="eager" />
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.townNight.credit}</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src={ASSETS.yuto.src} alt={ASSETS.yuto.alt} width={ASSETS.yuto.width} height={ASSETS.yuto.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="eager" />
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.yuto.credit}</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src={ASSETS.monsterAttack.src} alt={ASSETS.monsterAttack.alt} width={ASSETS.monsterAttack.width} height={ASSETS.monsterAttack.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="eager" />
          <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.monsterAttack.credit}</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <SourcePanel sources={CORE_SOURCES} />
      <FaqBlock items={homeFaqs} />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
